  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Clear workspace",
    "overview": "**Provisional scope: volunteer Home only.** This records the built Clear workspace proposal for `body.home-preview`, enabled only for a volunteer on `dashboard`. It is a review baseline, not an owner-approved site-wide system. Do not extend it to other routes before the owner reviews both directions and the working Home screen. Other screens continue to use `css/styles.css` and IBM Plex; Open agenda is a static alternative, not implemented app guidance.\n\nClear workspace is the proposal's working name, not an owner-selected brand commitment. The confirmed priorities are simplicity, readability, whitespace, order and contrast. The built screen expresses a campus student-services workspace through Public Sans, pale navigation, a white reading field, clear dates and explicit actions. Its first commitment leads; verified service and recommendations remain quieter. These composition choices describe this Home proposal only.\n\nSource authority is `volunteerhub-web/vh-web/css/home-preview.css` and `js/views/home-preview.js`, with inherited primitives from `css/styles.css` and scoped integration in `js/app.js` and `index.html`. The surface contract is `.impeccable/surfaces/volunteerhub-web-vh-web-js-views-home-preview-js.md` (`seed:d1036f369104af8f`). Token names are extraction keys, not new owner commitments. The frontmatter governs only this scope; dark suffixes record the source overrides. Sidecar tonal ramps are synthesized panel previews, not shipped token scales.\n\nThe finish verdict cleared four scored fixes: visible mobile destinations, underlined recommendation details, semantic progress in the alternate sketch, and complete city-origin copy in the dialog. It does not approve the whole surface or a site-wide rollout. The reported 34 isolated checks use sample data and stubbed Firebase configuration; they do not establish production Firebase or load-test readiness. See `docs/VISUAL_PREVIEW.md` for the two proposals and verification context.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Flat reading areas, pale navigation and restrained slate-blue actions.",
      "One UI family, tabular dates and service amounts, explicit action labels.",
      "Visible mobile destinations, inline display preferences and retained keyboard access.",
      "Text accompanies semantic progress and status color; no decorative imagery or shipped raster UI."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Semantic Progress Rule",
        "body": "Within this proposal, progress continuously mixes low red through midpoint yellow to completion green, with amounts and a percentage in text. Do not substitute a single accent fill.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One UI Family Rule",
        "body": "Public Sans carries Home headings, body text, dates, controls and dialog text. Other routes retain their existing typography until a separate owner decision.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Reading Surface Rule",
        "body": "Home content uses whitespace and divider rules at rest. Pop-up shadows belong to inherited dialogs and toasts, not to each shift or summary.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep this baseline confined to the volunteer Home proposal until the owner chooses the next scope.",
      "Do retain all five navigation destinations at rest on phones, with wrapping rather than clipped horizontal navigation.",
      "Do use explicit actions such as View shift, Find opportunities, View my hours and Sign up; keep recommendation titles visibly underlined at rest.",
      "Do preserve text size, Auto/Light/Dark, high contrast, reduced motion and keyboard focus behavior.",
      "Do retain numeric progress and clear service/status text alongside semantic color."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't treat Clear workspace, its extracted token names, the finish verdict or this file as owner style approval.",
      "Don't copy Open agenda's static composition into the app as an established system.",
      "Don't introduce neon accents, vague actions, descriptive tab clutter or unnecessary account dropdowns; the owner rejects SignUpGenius-style clutter.",
      "Don't replace working navigation, event IDs, data handlers or permission distinctions while applying visual changes."
    ]
  }
